# Row A1a: the Ward-compensated near/far round

This note records what was added in the near/far round of lane A1a
(`LiteralCompactSimplePositiveBeta`, half A1a), what is machine-checked, and
what precisely remains open. Every module named below was checked with
`agda --safe` (exit 0 for the module and its whole import cone) and contains no
postulate, hole, receipt or pragma.

## The idea

The four-orbit gate consumes a bound on the negative part of the single
(4,6,4,1)-weighted combination `D(p) = 4d₁(p)+6d₂(p)+4d₃(p)+d₄(p)` of the
literal joint Wilson + reduced Faddeev–Popov + Haar density. A uniform bound on
`D` is not available: the hard region is where the lattice propagator
denominator `p̂² = Σ_μ 4 sin²(p_μ/2)` is small.

The compensation principle used here is: **convert the exact cancellation into a
quantitative gain before taking absolute values.** Gauge invariance forces
transversality, `Π_{μν}(p) = (p̂²δ_{μν} − p̂_μ p̂_ν) Π(p)`, so the numerator of
the scalar quotient carries the same vanishing as the denominator. Factoring
that zero out first turns the dangerous region into a regular one; only then is
the region split into a near part (small, handled by the compensated bound) and
a far part (denominator floored, handled by the generic rational calculus).

## New modules

1. `DASHI/Physics/YangMills/BalabanCMP109LiteralWardCompensatedNearQuotientExact.agda`

   `NearRegion.wardFactoredQuotient`: if the numerator of a literal quotient is
   syntactically `multiply ward tilde` with `ward` evaluating to `h ≥ 0`, if
   `|tilde| ≤ m`, and if the denominator value `y > 0` satisfies the *same-zero
   comparison* `c·h ≤ y` with `c > 0`, then the quotient value `z` obeys

       |z| · c ≤ m .

   No denominator floor occurs anywhere in the statement, and the bound does not
   degrade as `h → 0`. Consumer forms (`wardFactoredModulusBound`,
   `wardFactoredNegativePart`), the weighted four-orbit near density bound, the
   literal instance with the inhabited inverse-propagator expression, and a
   machine-checked quantitative comparison with the generic `S/floor` route
   (which needs 30, 300, 3000 at floors 1/10, 1/100, 1/1000 where the
   compensated bound stays at 6) are included.

2. `DASHI/Physics/YangMills/BalabanCMP109LiteralOneLoopNearFarEstimateExact.agda`

   The assembly. A cell functional split into a near and a far part, each
   monotone only against comparisons valid on its own region:

   * `measureAdditivity` — the two region measures add up to the cell measure
     (derived, not assumed);
   * `nearFarLower` — `R ≥ −(measureNear·ε_near + measureFar·ε_far)` from
     region-restricted bounds only;
   * `splitMajorant` / `splitMajorantIntegral` /
     `literalJointRegularRemainderNearFar` — the two-valued majorant, its exact
